Good practices guide for loading and unloading of cryogenic liquid tankers — AIGA (@cs-aiga: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_52MNR8Y6S0N1MXDSX8F3XF424C
Asia Industrial Gases Association. Good practices guide for loading and unloading of cryogenic liquid tankers, AIGA 040/15. [Association-hosted full publication](https://asiaiga.org/uploaded_docs/en_AIGA_040_15_Guide__loading_and_Unloading_of_Cryo_Liquid_Tankers.pdf).

Read the full guide to connect production storage, tanker logistics and customer bulk tanks, using its stated oxygen/nitrogen/argon and grade scope. Identify what each party must know at a transfer and which responsibilities cross the organizational boundary. Production/separation processes themselves are outside this guide's stated scope.

The official indexed document supplied its identity and scope on 29 October 2026; direct retrieval then failed. On 30 October the association URL without www returned the full fourteen-page PDF with valid TLS. Its cover, contents, permission notice and selected quality, traceability and quantity passages were inspected. AIGA grants reproduction with acknowledgement; this is not an unrestricted adaptation licence. The www hostname had a certificate mismatch, so the working official URL is linked above. Keep the actual edition and notice when consulting it. Gas-specific installation design and operating competence require the relevant complete technical programme. All source material remains external.

